### 🔴 Critical #2 — Missing Edge-Case / Error-Path Tests

The production code has real failure modes that no test exercises:

| Untested behavior | Production code (line) | Risk |
|---|---|---|
| `UpdatePrice` on missing SKU | `throw new KeyNotFoundException(sku)` (L14) | Callers may not know this throws |
| `ImportFromCsv` with malformed input | `decimal.Parse(parts[2])` (L33) | Will throw `FormatException` / `IndexOutOfRangeException` |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount` with fraction ≥ 1 | Prices go to zero or negative (L24) | Business logic bug in production |
| `Search` with empty/null query | Behavior is unspecified | Potential `NullReferenceException` |

**Example fix — verify the exception contract:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_MissingSku_ThrowsKeyNotFoundException()
{
    Assert.ThrowsException<KeyNotFoundException>(
        () => _catalog.UpdatePrice("NONEXISTENT", 5.00m));
}
```

